// Sound/Dialogue/UndeadRebirth/UndeadRE01/UndeadRE01Cin06Anya01.mp3
{
This is the dreadlord Varimathras. Defector from the Scourge, now a servant of the Dark Lady.
}

STRING 2482
// Sound/Dialogue/UndeadRebirth/UndeadRE01/URE01Cin06Anya02.mp3
{
Good of you to finally show up. Where have you been?
}

STRING 2483
// Sound/Dialogue/UndeadRebirth/UndeadRE01/URE01Cin06Varimathras01.mp3
{
Investigating this incursion. The Scourge have been digging tunnels through the old catacombs.
}

STRING 2484
// Sound/Dialogue/UndeadRebirth/UndeadRE01/UndeadRE01Cin06Varimathras02.mp3
{
What you fought here was merely a scouting force. I command you to exterminate the rest of them.
}

STRING 2485
// Sound/Dialogue/UndeadRebirth/UndeadRE01/URE01Cin06Anya03.mp3
{
That may prove difficult for just the two of us.
}

STRING 2486
// Sound/Dialogue/UndeadRebirth/UndeadRE01/UndeadRE01Cin06Varimathras03.mp3
{
Then recruit more soldiers and form a city guard. Whatever your course of action, do it quickly. I am not as patient as Lady Sylvanas.
}

STRING 2505
{
Telling the player that this is point of non return
}

STRING 2506
{
Their leader spoke of a cathedral. That must be their base of operations, and how they gained access to these corridors.
}

STRING 2507
{
We’ll follow these tunnels, infiltrate the cathedral and kill whoever we find there.
}

STRING 2508
{
The priest that was with these soldiers... he seemed to understand that the Forsaken differ from the Scourge.
}

STRING 2509
{
Do you suppose, if we find him in the cathedral, that we can reason with him?
}

STRING 2510
{
Absolutely not. Never trust the living, Garek. They are the enemy.
}

STRING 2511
{
If you insist, Anya.
}

STRING 2512
{
Introducing the Blind Forsaken Quest
}

STRING 2513
{
Hello? Who’s there? I can’t see without my eye!
}

STRING 2514
{
Edric? What are you doing down here?
}

STRING 2515
{
Anya, is that you? I lost my one good eye and now I can’t find my way out of the sewers!
}

STRING 2516
{
Well, your chances of finding it are pretty slim. Stay here for now.
}

STRING 2517
{
Introducing the Ghouls Quest
}

STRING 2518
{
Hmm. Do you believe ghouls are capable of sentience, despite the state of their cerebral matter?
}

STRING 2519
{
This again, Keever? Ghouls are mindless beasts, driven only by hunger.
}

STRING 2520
{
A common assumption. One that Keever must prove or disprove.
}

STRING 2521
{
There are reports of ghouls nearby who exhibit unusual behavior. Bring them to Keever for observation.
}

STRING 2522
{
Introducing the Arcane Sanctuary Quest
}

STRING 2523
{
Anya, Sir Bandaron, I could very much benefit from your assistance.
}

STRING 2524
{
You see, I recently discovered that hidden with the ruins of the Capital City is the entrance to an arcane vault.
}

STRING 2525
{
I surmise that said vault may contain all manner of powerful artifacts once used by the Menethil’s own royal mages.
}

STRING 2526
{
I dare not brave the ruins myself, let along the vault. But if you were to do so for me...
}

STRING 2527
{
We’ll see what we can do. But if this ends up being a wild goose chase, there will be hell to pay.
}

STRING 2528
{
Introducing the Abomination Quest
}

STRING 2529
{
Putress has tasked Keever with assembling a new abomination. But we need another batch of parts.
}

STRING 2530
{
Apparently, the parts Keever was supposed to use rather rudely woke up and started walking around.
}

STRING 2531
{
Sorry to have caused you such an inconvenience.
}

STRING 2532
{
Hmph. Keever has compiled a list of suitable replacements. Can you manage collecting them?
}

STRING 2533
{
I suppose it’s the least I could do. Let’s have the list, then.
}

STRING 2534
{
Plague Canals Quest Cinematic
}

STRING 2535
{
Anya, Garek. You’ve done well bringing more Forsaken into the Undercity. As our population grows, so too do our chances at survival.
}

STRING 2536
{
Unfortunately, we have also become a larger target for those who seek to destroy us. Intruders have been spotted in the city’s canals.
}

STRING 2537
{
You are to poison the water supply with plague. Such toxins won’t harm the Forsaken, but will discourage the living from further trespassing.
}

STRING 2538
{
It will be done, Dark Lady.
}

